## How to use parameters in your script?

# TL;DR: copy function to your script. reference parameters as shown below.
we mount all generic/useful secrets to all pods (i.e ARTIFACTORY_TOKEN, GIT_TOKEN). check out """"""""""" for your existing secrets. if you want to add a new secret, ask team genesys for help.
the function check if your parameter exists in secrets, if not it uses a regular parameter (that the user passed when he ran the script) 

# python
    
```python
import os

def get_param(name):
    path = f"/etc/eden-secrets/{name}"
    try:
        with open(path) as f:
            return f.read().strip() # it is a secret
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return os.getenv(name) # it is a simple parameter

# refernce parameters:
artifactory_token = get_param("ARTIFACTORY_TOKEN")
username = get_param("username")
```

# bash

```bash
get_param() {
  local name=$1
  local path="/etc/eden-secrets/$name"
  if [ -f "$path" ]; then
    cat "$path" # it is a secret
  else
    echo "${!name}"  # it is a parameter
  fi
}

# reference parameters:
ARTIFACTORY_TOKEN=$(get_param "ARTIFACTORY_TOKEN")
username=$(get_param "username")

```

# Powershell

```powershell

function Get-Param($name) {
    $path = "/etc/eden-secrets/$name"
    if (Test-Path $path) {
        return (Get-Content $path -Raw).Trim() # it is a secret
    }
    return $env:$name  # it is a parameter
}

# reference parameters:
$artifactoryToken = Get-Param "ARTIFACTORY_TOKEN"
$userName = Get-Param "userName"

```

